  {
    client: "Aleido Learning",
    meta: "Sweden · 2015–2025 · Moodle / Totara / Laravel",
    body: "Engineered the technical solution for large LMS migrations for Swedish regional government, including one of 800,000 users and several million enrolments. Built an enrolment plugin in 2015 that I maintained and extended until 2023, by which point it was a core part of the product. On one upgrade the client credited my code quality for development hours coming in significantly under estimate.",
    link: null,
    linkLabel: null,
  },
  {
    client: "mod_goodhabits",
    meta: "Public Moodle plugin · PHP",
    body: "An actively used activity plugin in the official Moodle plugin directory — designed, built and maintained by me. If you want to read my code before hiring me, start here.",
    link: "https://moodle.org/plugins/mod_goodhabits",
    linkLabel: "View on moodle.org →",
  },
  {
    client: "Talking Mats Ltd.",
    meta: "Stirling · 2011–present · Moodle consultant",
    body: "Built the organisation's original Moodle system in 2011 — work the client credited in part for winning Start Up Social Enterprise of the Year in 2012. Fifteen years on they're still running it as a core income stream, and I still advise on it. Their summary is that it 'just works' with minimal maintenance.",
    link: null,
    linkLabel: null,
  },
  {
    client: "Royal Holloway, University of London",
    meta: "Surrey · 2017–2018 · Moodle consultant",
    body: "Managed a major platform upgrade, course rollover and archiving cycle synchronised with a Windows Server migration, for a campus of 12,000+ students and 1,800 staff. Load-tested with JMeter to keep downtime to a minimum.",
    link: null,
    linkLabel: null,
  },
];
---

<section class="section section-dark">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Selected work</span>
    <h2 class="section-title reveal">Fifteen years of it holding up</h2>
    <p class="section-lead reveal">
      The pattern that matters most in this work isn't the launch — it's what
      the system looks like five years later.
    </p>

    <div class="proof-grid">
      {
        work.map((item) => (
          <article class="proof-item reveal">
            <h3>{item.client}</h3>
            <p class="proof-meta">{item.meta}</p>
            <p>{item.body}</p>
            {item.link && (
              <a class="proof-link" href={item.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                {item.linkLabel}
              </a>
            )}
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="proof-note reveal">
      Earlier, as a developer at <strong>Epic Ltd. / LEO Learning</strong> and the
       <strong> University of London Computer Centre</strong>, I was lead technical
      developer on Moodle systems for Aviva plc, the Nursing &amp; Midwifery
      Council and the Glasgow 2014 Commonwealth Games, and helped builed the
       <a href="https://moodle.org/plugins/view.php?id=610" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> Individual Learning Planner </a>
      add-on for Moodle. I also built core backend features of
      <a href="https://pi-datametrics.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> Pi Datametrics </a>
      and launched <a href="https://squiddity.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Squiddity</a>,
      my own Flutter app for iOS and Android.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
